  "notes": "{期待|きたい} means \"expectation\" or \"hope\"—anticipating something positive will happen. Can function as a noun or する verb.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を{期待|きたい}する: to expect ~, to hope for ~\n- {期待|きたい}に{応|こた}える: to meet/live up to expectations\n- {期待|きたい}を{裏切|うらぎ}る: to betray expectations\n- {期待|きたい}はずれ: disappointment, letdown\n- {期待|きたい}が{高|たか}まる: expectations rise\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {期待|きたい}しています: I'm looking forward to it\n- ご{期待|きたい}ください: Please look forward to it (promotional)\n- {期待|きたい}どおり: as expected\n\nUSAGE NOTE: {期待|きたい} usually implies positive anticipation, unlike 予想 (yosou) which is more neutral.",
